1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,330
I have to admit I'm a little bit nervous because this is our first overnight hike together.
我得承认，有点紧张，因为这是我们第一次一起过夜徒步。

2
00:00:06,330 --> 00:00:15,810
I mean not my first overnight hike but vilk's and I have no idea what he's gonna what he's gonna make of it.
我是说，不是我第一次过夜徒步，而是 Vilk 的第一次。我完全不知道他会怎么看待这件事。

3
00:00:15,810 --> 00:00:23,400
A few days prior to this hike I found a pioneer cabin on a local trail map and decided that I'd like to go and check it out.
徒步前几天，我在当地路线地图上找到一间拓荒者小屋，决定想去看看。

4
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:30,390
But it's high up in the mountains and it's still early in the season so I knew there might be a lot of snow up there.
但小屋在很高的山上，而且季节还早，我知道上面可能有很多雪。

5
00:00:30,390 --> 00:00:33,930
The idea today is try to get as far as I can.
今天的想法就是，尽自己所能走远一点。

6
00:00:38,132 --> 00:00:41,700
Isn't it a bit too big for you you don't think so.
这对你来说是不是太大了？你不觉得吗？

7
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:51,560
You gonna bring it come on let's go come on let's go jesus vilk.
你要带上它吗？来吧，走吧，来，走吧。天哪，Vilk。

8
00:00:52,923 --> 00:01:00,930
Even out there in the wild far from phone calls and to do lists I still sometimes find it hard to switch off.
即使在野外，远离电话和待办清单，我有时还是觉得很难放松、停止操心。

9
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:07,773
And then there's this guy loving every single moment so present just so full of joy.
可这个家伙享受每一刻，那么专注当下，充满快乐。

10
00:01:08,670 --> 00:01:13,053
We could probably learn a lot from our furry friends if only we looked closely enough.
如果我们仔细观察，也许能从毛茸茸的朋友身上学到很多。

11
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:23,370
You know over the last couple of years I've kind of thought of hiking as fun but not exactly thrilling anymore.
过去几年，我觉得徒步有趣，但已经不算特别令人兴奋。

12
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:31,650
Because I guess I got a little bit used to it I did a lot of it and then it stopped being this exciting new thing.
大概因为我有点习惯了，走得太多，就不再是令人兴奋的新鲜事。

13
00:01:31,650 --> 00:01:40,590
But now that I have vilk and now that I'm hiking with him all of a sudden it's exciting again.
但现在有了 Vilk，我和他一起徒步，突然又觉得兴奋起来。

14
00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:49,280
Because he added a whole new level of challenge into hiking I gotta keep him fed and safe and healthy and happy.
因为他为徒步增加了全新的挑战，我得让他吃饱、平安、健康、开心。

15
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:55,953
And in a way that's kind of rekindled my passion for hiking which is great.
这在某种程度上重新点燃了我对徒步的热情，很棒。

16
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:04,230
I would imagine this is what happens when yeah when you get kids or when you get a pet or when you enter a new relationship.
我想，当你有了孩子、养宠物，或者进入一段新关系时，也会这样。

17
00:02:04,230 --> 00:02:15,843
All of a sudden you get a new perspective on things let's go ooh steep steep steep.
突然，你会换个角度看事情。走吧，哦，好陡，好陡，好陡。

18
00:02:32,441 --> 00:02:39,920
The snow is too soft it literally takes like 30 seconds to make a single step.
雪太软了，真的差不多每走一步都要三十秒。

19
00:02:45,420 --> 00:02:51,207
Snow shoes anyone anyone snow shoes.
雪鞋，有人有吗？有人吗？雪鞋？

20
00:02:53,190 --> 00:02:57,750
There's a rule in the climbing and hiking world and that rule is turnaround time.
登山和徒步圈里有个规则，就是折返时间。

21
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:07,500
I'm tempted to keep going just cause of that you know that ego telling me that I can make it and that I shouldn't give up.
我很想继续走，因为内心的自尊告诉我，我能做到，不该放弃。

22
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:11,970
But the snow is so deep it's just it's a nightmare.
但雪实在太深了，简直是噩梦。

23
00:03:11,970 --> 00:03:19,290
It's a time that you agree to where no matter how close you may be to the summit if you still haven't made it you must turn around.
这是你预先定下的时间，不管离山顶多近，如果还没到，就得折返。

24
00:03:19,290 --> 00:03:22,860
This is to avoid getting stuck in the dark or in dangerous conditions.
这样是为了避免天黑或危险环境中被困。

25
00:03:22,860 --> 00:03:31,047
Well my turnaround time was about to arrive and the storm clouds in the distance oh yeah they motivated me to turn around even faster.
我的折返时间就快到了，远处的暴风云又让我更想赶紧回头。

26
00:03:31,047 --> 00:03:38,250
Vilk is loving it but I am not and I'm not too sure about it I mean it feels a little bit fishy to me.
Vilk 很享受，可我没有。我也不太确定，这感觉有点不对劲。

27
00:03:38,250 --> 00:03:43,410
So I think what I'm gonna do is I'm not gonna go all the way to the end of the trail.
所以我想，我不会一直走到路线尽头了。

28
00:03:43,410 --> 00:03:53,040
I'm gonna turn back and we're gonna set up camp a little bit lower down where it's not so freaking annoying.
我要往回走，在低一点、没这么让人烦躁的地方扎营。

29
00:03:55,350 --> 00:03:58,380
Yep no regrets turning around.
对，回头一点都不后悔。

30
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:03,090
I watched a youtube video a few months back where someone was running a race in the mountains.
几个月前我看了个视频，有人在山里跑比赛。

31
00:04:03,090 --> 00:04:08,460
He was disappointed with his performance and found the run too boring to even make into a video.
他对表现失望，觉得这次跑步太无聊，都不值得做成视频。

32
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:13,246
But see he had brought his dog along for the run and watching his dog made him realize that.
但他带了狗去跑，看着狗，他意识到……

33
00:04:13,246 --> 00:04:18,420
Not every run needs to be extraordinary and something to write home about.
不是每次跑步都得非同寻常、值得大书特书。

34
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:27,960
Sometimes you just go for a run or a hike I mean you know at the end of the day the most important thing is that we have fun while hiking.
有时就只是去跑一跑、走一走。说到底，最重要的是徒步时开心。

35
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:37,540
And we push ourselves a little bit but not to the point where it becomes dangerous and you just enjoy it in the moment and that is all that matters.
也稍微挑战自己，但别到危险程度，享受当下，这就够了。

36
00:04:38,730 --> 00:04:43,350
Look at him this is vilk's famous ambush pose.
看他，这是 Vilk 著名的埋伏姿势。

37
00:04:43,530 --> 00:04:48,466
He's about to ambush me the closer I get look at this check this out now.
我越靠近，他就越准备扑我。看，看这个，现在。
